# .gitignore — keeps `git add .` from sweeping in ~114 MB of generated data.
#
# This file only affects files that are NOT already tracked. It deletes
# nothing, changes no history, and can be removed at any time with no effect
# on your work.
#
# Rule of thumb: source and evidence are tracked; anything a script can
# regenerate is not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data — the reason committing felt dangerous.
# cat_outputs/ alone is 421 files / 114 MB, including a 42 MB NetCDF.
# Patterns are by extension rather than by folder, so the small result CSVs
# in cat_outputs/ (summary_stats.csv, comparison_table.csv) STAY TRACKED.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.nc
*.grib
*.grb
*.idx
*.zarr/
*.tmp

# The verification input is small (687 KB) and makes the verification
# reproducible by anyone who clones this — keep it despite the *.nc rule.
!era5_validation_subset.nc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials — never commit these. Your CDS API key lives in .cdsapirc.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cdsapirc
.cdsapirc_*
*.key
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pixi/          # pixi builds the environment here, inside the repo
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HPC / SLURM run artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   verification/   — the evidence that the diagnostics are correct. This is
#                     the whole point of phase 0; it must be in the repo.
#   *.csv           — small result tables worth keeping under version control.
#   5_explore.ipynb — real work. It is 2.6 MB because the plot outputs are
#                     saved inside it; clearing outputs before committing
#                     drops it to a few KB, but that is your call, not mine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
